 President of the United  States might pay attention to what's  going on and also think about resigning  but if your point is that it's not just  Alf Rankin you're absolutely right but I  do want to talk about the absurd tax  proposal that the Republicans pass  on Friday night and I think what your  poll tells us is the American people got  it right and what the American people  understand is that this legislation is a  gift to the largest corporations in this  country who are already doing  phenomenally well in to the wealthiest  people 62% of the benefits in the  Republican Senate tax proposal goes to  the top one percent and large  corporations and at the end of ten years  we're gonna have some 80 million  Americans middle-class Americans paying  more in taxes so in the midst of massive  income and wealth inequality we give tax  breaks to billionaires raise taxes on  the middle class but you're evil but  you're going about that where your point  about it going to is because the  corporate tax rate because what the  Republicans are proposing is that it  would go from thirty five percent to  twenty percent to be fair President  Obama also proposed a reduction in the  corporate tax rate but to about twenty  eight percent are you saying that those  businesses won't reinvest that money in  American businesses and American workers  yes of course that's what I'm saying and  I think that's what they are saying if  anybody thinks that this is going to  result in higher wages and more jobs in  America I don't believe that that's the  case this is trickle-down economic  theory it is a theory that did not work  on the Reagan did not work on the George  W Bush certainly did not work in Kansas  but here's the other point this  legislation drove up the deficit by one  point four trillion dollars and now what  Paul Ryan and other Republican leaders  are saying oh my goodness the deficit  has gone up we have to deal with that  crisis and you know how they're gonna do  it read the front page of the New York  Times the other day they are going to  now come back and cut Social Security  Medicare Medicaid and education so what  this whole thing is about tax breaks for  billionaires and cuts to programs for  the most vulnerable people in this  country and let me also add some people  may remember that during the campaign  candidate Donald Trump he said I'm not  going to cut Social Security Medicare  and Medicaid remember those statements  said it over and over again  well I challenge President Trump today  to tell the Republican leadership that  he will veto any legislation that comes  forward  contradicts the promises that he made to  the American people in terms of Social  Security Medicare and Medicaid  senator another issue at hand is keeping  the government open and keeping it  funded it looks like there will be a  stop-gap plan in place for the next two  weeks but Congress is nowhere near a  permanent deal you have said that you  will not vote for a spending bill  without a permanent fix for dreamers the  president said that if there is a  government shutdown it's gonna be the  Democrats fault are you willing to take  that responsibility no it's certainly  not going to be the Democrats fault let  us all remember last I heard Republicans  control the US Senate Republicans  control the US House and right now what  is going on is Republicans want huge  increases for military spending but they  don't want to provide another nickel to  make sure that we can lower student  loans in this country that we could deal  with the crisis of pensions in this  country right now 10,000 people died  last year because they couldn't get  their claims processed by the Social  Security Administration where funds have  gone down we have enormous issues that  we have got to deal with and instead of  giving tax breaks to billionaires maybe  a time the Republican Party started  looking at the needs of the working  class and middle class of this country  but in 2013 in the shutdown then you  said it is wrong for right-wing  Republicans to ignore the results of the  last election and hold the American  people hostage by threatening to shut  down the government because they can't  get their way what makes this different  some people walking you assuming that we  are shutting down the government we want  to keep who wants to shut down the  government I don't want to shut down the  government I don't know if anybody will  make you a kondal said that this isn't a  pressing issue you still have three  months ago Mitch McConnell said that all  I forgot last I heard Mitch McConnell  was the leader of the Republican Party  who just passed tax breaks that give  they just passed tax breaks for  billionaires and tried to throw 32  million Americans or for the health  insurance they have there will be  negotiations and I hope very much these  negotiations were resolved but we cannot  in the midst of giving tax breaks to  people who don't need it in the midst of  trying to throw millions of people off  the health insurance forget about the  needs of the working class in this  country and the middle class which is  shrinking you know what politics is  about  it's not just doing what you wealthy  campaign contributors want you to do  it's paying attention to ordinary people  all right senator Sanders we're gonna  have to leave it there we thank you very  much for joining us should be a very  interesting day on Capitol Hill today  thanks a lot thank you
 

